From 8bf8305059747b35a5fe0070bf190c22b7784d42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:51:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 45/51] Add the learning center: reading shelf, word book page,
 cache cleanup

The learning resources - the bilingual reading list and the word
book - were buried under the subtitle settings, and the word book had
no page at all: words could be saved, but nowhere to be seen. The
settings now carry a first-level Learning center entry with the two
resources side by side.

The reading shelf: a cached subtitle can be moved onto it from the
cache list's action menu (the cache entry now opens an action menu
instead of jumping straight into the viewer). Shelved subtitles are
exempt from the automatic cleanup, so reading material survives;
taking one off the shelf returns it to plain cache semantics.

The word book page: one compact card per saved word - the word, its
phonetic transcription, a preview of the definition and the save
date. Tapping a card opens the shared dictionary popup, and the
popup now reads the stored definition first: saving a word stores
the entry of the finished lookup with it (and a lookup finishing
after an early save backfills it), so browsing the book costs no
requests, hits no rate limit and works offline. Words saved before
this cache existed are fetched on demand and backfilled.

The cache cleanup: a switch (on by default) and a threshold (10 to
1000, default 100) in the subtitle settings. When the cache list
opens, the oldest unpinned entries beyond the threshold are deleted.

Backup coverage: the word book (with the stored definitions), the
reading shelf and the cleanup settings all live in the default
shared preferences, so they ride along in every export and cloud
backup without any backup-side change - the subtitle files
themselves have been part of the backup since patch 0029.
